{
  "A scrollable container with configurable scrollbars, pull-to-refresh, and load-on-scroll near the end of the content. You can scroll it programmatically to a position or an element.": "",
  "Scrollable content": "",
  "JSX children are the content. `showScrollbar` sets when scrollbars appear. `scrollTo` and `scrollToElement` scroll programmatically, and `onScrolled` reports the position.": "",
  "Pull to refresh": "Çekerek yenileme",
  "With `pullToRefresh`, pulling the content down from the top raises `onPullDown`. Set `promise`, or call `release()`, and the panel closes when the work is finished.": "",
  "Load more": "",
  "With `loadOnReachBottom`, scrolling within `reachBottomOffset` of the end raises `onReachBottom` once. `release()` allows the next request, and `release(true)` signals that there is no more data. Content that does not fill the view requests more immediately.": "",
  "The box scrolls with the mouse wheel, the keyboard when focused, touch, and code. `direction` locks the other axis, and the page behind does not continue scrolling when the content ends.": "",
  "These are the design system scrollbars. With `onScroll`, the thumb appears while the content moves and hides shortly after. With `onHover`, it appears while the pointer is over the view or focus is inside it. `always` keeps it visible, and `never` hides it while the content still scrolls.": "",
  "From the top, with a finger or the pointer, the content moves down with increasing resistance, and the panel above it prompts the user to pull and then release. Releasing far enough starts a refresh, and the spinner runs until `release()` or the promise. A short pull returns to its position.": "",
  "Within `reachBottomOffset` of the end, `onReachBottom` is raised once, and the panel below the content is shown meanwhile. After release, the next approach raises it again, until `release(true)`. Content that does not fill the box requests more immediately, and again as it grows.": "",
  "The kit strings in the kit language, unless the text props override them.": "",
  "A focusable box named by `label`. The arrow keys, Page Up, Page Down, Home and End scroll it, using the browser's default behavior.": "",
  "Live regions announce “Refreshing…” and “Loading…” when they appear.": "",
  "Decorative. The text describes what is happening.": "",
  "A finger that pulls does not scroll the page, and a finger that scrolls does not pull.": "",
  "The box. `data-direction`, `data-bars`, `data-scrolling` while the content moves, `data-pull` when pull-to-refresh is on, `data-pulling` during a pull, `data-pull-state` (`pull`, `release`, `refreshing`) and `data-loading`.": "",
  "The element that holds the children, which moves down during a pull.": "",
  "The panel above the content, its text and the kit spinner.": "",
  "The panel below the content while more data loads.": "",
  "Unit: the box (`focus`).": "Unit: kutu (`focus`).",
  "Units: the two panels (the pull panel has `release` and `refreshing`) and their text.": "",
  "The height of the panels, and the space between a panel's spinner and its text.": "",
  "`vertical`, `horizontal` or `both`: the scroll direction.": "",
  "When scrollbars appear: `onScroll` while scrolling, `onHover` while the pointer is over the view, `always` or `never`.": "",
  "Pulling the content down from the top raises `onPullDown`.": "",
  "Scrolling near the end raises `onReachBottom`, as does content that does not reach the end.": "",
  "The distance from the end, in pixels, at which `onReachBottom` is raised.": "",
  "The kit strings": "",
  "The pull panel text: while pulling, once far enough, and while refreshing.": "",
  "The text below the content while more data loads.": "",
  "The accessible name of the scrolling region.": "",
  "Occurs when the content is pulled down and released. Load the new data and call `release()`, or set `promise` and the panel closes when it settles.": "",
  "Occurs when the content is scrolled near its end. Load more data and call `release()`. `release(true)` signals that there is no more data, and the view stops requesting. A `promise` also releases it.": "",
  "Occurs when the position changes: `top`, `left`.": "",
  "Scrolls to a top position, or to `{ top, left }`. `smooth` animates the scroll.": "",
  "Scrolls by a distance.": "",
  "Scrolls an element or component of the content into view.": "",
  "Starts a refresh as a pull would, or ends it.": "",
  "Requests more data now, or checks the position again after the content changes.": "",
  "The current scroll position.": "",
  "Indicates that a refresh or a load is in progress.": "",
  "The element that holds the children, between the two panels.": "İki panel arasında alt öğeleri tutan öğe."
}
